UID:ec2dc322f06287ef@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair 
 and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHA
 NGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal 
 are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP
  for Seraphs: Angels - Seraphs — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless 
 Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup
 : Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provid
 es): Gold Halo headpiece\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• 
  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shadow applied to the
  crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and 
 black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to 
 apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n
 •  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone t
 ights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Ha
 ndle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delica
 te fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of cost
 ume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• 
  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes 
 by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while
  in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder
  any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in co
 stume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on cost
 ume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or
  cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned t
 o cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while i
 n costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes 
 from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove a
 ll bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 •  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply ful
 ly with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•
   Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may 
 damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
