SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATO
 RY — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be chec
 k-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance
  Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is name
 d. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails a
 nd the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.co
 m/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUM
 E / HAIR / MAKEUP for Seraphs: Angels - Seraphs — Costume (you provide
 ): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ball
 et Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Acces
 sories (BA provides): Gold Halo headpiece\nLight Stage Makeup Instructio
 n Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye shad
 ow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/Bl
 ack eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the ch
 eeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the
  stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may w
 ear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guideli
 nes:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent 
 damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in t
 he event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how sig
 nificant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or 
 hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on t
 he floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clea
 n\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-
 up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging m
 ake-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of sp
 ray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment 
 not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or be
 verage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not re
 move costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n
 •  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs follow
 ing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•
   Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrob
 e policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or any
 thing that may damage or stain costumes.
